<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">17 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 17 January, from 1377 to 1995.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1377 CE <span class="tih-ago">649 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Gregory XI returns the papacy to Rome</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Urged on by Catherine of Siena, Gregory XI entered Rome, ending almost seven decades in which the popes had lived at Avignon. His death the next year set off the Great Western Schism.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1773 CE <span class="tih-ago">253 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">James Cook makes the first recorded crossing of the Antarctic Circle</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">HMS Resolution and HMS Adventure sailed south of 66°33' S, the first ships known to do so. Cook's voyage showed that any southern continent must lie far to the south, beyond the pack ice.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1781 CE <span class="tih-ago">245 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Daniel Morgan routs Tarleton at the Battle of Cowpens</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In South Carolina, Daniel Morgan's Continentals and militia destroyed Banastre Tarleton's British force with a skilful double envelopment. The victory was a turning point in the southern campaign.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/united-states" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-states.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1893 CE <span class="tih-ago">133 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hawaii's Queen Liliuokalani overthrown</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A committee of American and European businessmen, supported by US Marines from the USS Boston, deposed the Hawaiian queen and set up a provisional government. The United States annexed Hawaii in 1898.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1945 CE <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soviet and Polish troops enter the ruins of Warsaw</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Red Army and the Polish First Army took Warsaw, abandoned by the Germans. After the crushing of the 1944 Uprising, the Germans had systematically razed the city, destroying about 85 per cent of it.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1946 CE <span class="tih-ago">80 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">UN Security Council meets for the first time</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The United Nations Security Council held its first session at Church House, Westminster. Its five permanent members, each with a veto, were the United States, the Soviet Union, Britain, France and China.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1961 CE <span class="tih-ago">65 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Eisenhower warns of the 'military-industrial complex'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In his televised farewell address, the outgoing President cautioned that a permanent arms industry and huge defence establishment could acquire 'unwarranted influence' over American government.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1991 CE <span class="tih-ago">35 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Operation Desert Storm opens with air strikes on Iraq</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A US-led coalition began a massive air campaign against Iraq, which had occupied Kuwait since August 1990. A ground offensive in late February expelled Iraqi forces within 100 hours.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1995 CE <span class="tih-ago">31 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Great Hanshin earthquake devastates Kobe</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A magnitude 6.9 earthquake struck the Kobe region before dawn, killing 6,434 people and destroying over 100,000 buildings. The slow official response prompted reform of Japan's disaster planning.</p></div></li></ol>
